{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"rehype-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rehype API"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/highlight/rehype"},{"type":"text","value":" transforms existing HAST "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<pre><code>"},{"type":"text","value":" pairs. It has no dependency on Rehype itself."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rehypehighlightoptions","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RehypeHighlightOptions"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type RehypeHighlightOptions = {\n  highlighter: Highlighter\n  lineNumbers?: boolean\n  getDecorations?: (node: HastElement) =>\n    ReadonlyArray<HighlightDecoration> | undefined\n  getTitle?: (node: HastElement) => string | undefined\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Callbacks receive the original "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pre"},{"type":"text","value":" node. Language names are read from a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"language-*"},{"type":"text","value":" class on the child "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code"},{"type":"text","value":" element."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fence titles, annotations, and line numbers are read from the child code node's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data.meta"},{"type":"text","value":", as emitted by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mdast-util-to-hast"},{"type":"text","value":". A callback title or explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lineNumbers"},{"type":"text","value":" option overrides metadata."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rehypehighlightcodeblocks","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rehypeHighlightCodeBlocks"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function rehypeHighlightCodeBlocks(\n  options: RehypeHighlightOptions,\n): (tree: unknown) => void","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a synchronous Rehype transformer. It recursively replaces supported "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<pre><code>"},{"type":"text","value":" nodes and skips any "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pre"},{"type":"text","value":" that already has the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"th-code"},{"type":"text","value":" class."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import rehypeStringify from 'rehype-stringify'\nimport remarkParse from 'remark-parse'\nimport remarkRehype from 'remark-rehype'\nimport { unified } from 'unified'\nimport { rehypeHighlightCodeBlocks } from '@tanstack/highlight/rehype'\n\nconst file = await unified()\n  .use(remarkParse)\n  .use(remarkRehype)\n  .use(rehypeHighlightCodeBlocks, { highlighter })\n  .use(rehypeStringify)\n  .process(markdown)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rehypeprecodetohast","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rehypePreCodeToHast"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function rehypePreCodeToHast(\n  node: HastElement,\n  options: RehypeHighlightOptions,\n): HastElement | undefined","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Converts one eligible "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pre"},{"type":"text","value":" node. It returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" when the node is already highlighted or does not contain a direct "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code"},{"type":"text","value":" child. Descendant text is concatenated and trailing whitespace is removed before highlighting."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Existing attributes, classes, and plugin data on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pre"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code"},{"type":"text","value":" elements are preserved."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../guides/markdown-pipelines","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Markdown Pipelines"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for choosing between the Remark and Rehype integrations."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"rehype-api","text":"Rehype API","level":1},{"id":"rehypehighlightoptions","text":"RehypeHighlightOptions","level":2},{"id":"rehypehighlightcodeblocks","text":"rehypeHighlightCodeBlocks","level":2},{"id":"rehypeprecodetohast","text":"rehypePreCodeToHast","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Rehype API\n\n`@tanstack/highlight/rehype` transforms existing HAST `<pre><code>` pairs. It has no dependency on Rehype itself.\n\n## `RehypeHighlightOptions`\n\n```ts\ntype RehypeHighlightOptions = {\n  highlighter: Highlighter\n  lineNumbers?: boolean\n  getDecorations?: (node: HastElement) =>\n    ReadonlyArray<HighlightDecoration> | undefined\n  getTitle?: (node: HastElement) => string | undefined\n}\n```\n\nCallbacks receive the original `pre` node. Language names are read from a `language-*` class on the child `code` element.\n\nFence titles, annotations, and line numbers are read from the child code node's `data.meta`, as emitted by `mdast-util-to-hast`. A callback title or explicit `lineNumbers` option overrides metadata.\n\n## `rehypeHighlightCodeBlocks`\n\n```ts\nfunction rehypeHighlightCodeBlocks(\n  options: RehypeHighlightOptions,\n): (tree: unknown) => void\n```\n\nReturns a synchronous Rehype transformer. It recursively replaces supported `<pre><code>` nodes and skips any `pre` that already has the `th-code` class.\n\n```ts\nimport rehypeStringify from 'rehype-stringify'\nimport remarkParse from 'remark-parse'\nimport remarkRehype from 'remark-rehype'\nimport { unified } from 'unified'\nimport { rehypeHighlightCodeBlocks } from '@tanstack/highlight/rehype'\n\nconst file = await unified()\n  .use(remarkParse)\n  .use(remarkRehype)\n  .use(rehypeHighlightCodeBlocks, { highlighter })\n  .use(rehypeStringify)\n  .process(markdown)\n```\n\n## `rehypePreCodeToHast`\n\n```ts\nfunction rehypePreCodeToHast(\n  node: HastElement,\n  options: RehypeHighlightOptions,\n): HastElement | undefined\n```\n\nConverts one eligible `pre` node. It returns `undefined` when the node is already highlighted or does not contain a direct `code` child. Descendant text is concatenated and trailing whitespace is removed before highlighting.\n\nExisting attributes, classes, and plugin data on the `pre` and `code` elements are preserved.\n\nSee [Markdown Pipelines](../guides/markdown-pipelines) for choosing between the Remark and Rehype integrations.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Rehype API\n---\n\n# Rehype API\n\n`@tanstack/highlight/rehype` transforms existing HAST `<pre><code>` pairs. It has no dependency on Rehype itself.\n\n## `RehypeHighlightOptions`\n\n```ts\ntype RehypeHighlightOptions = {\n  highlighter: Highlighter\n  lineNumbers?: boolean\n  getDecorations?: (node: HastElement) =>\n    ReadonlyArray<HighlightDecoration> | undefined\n  getTitle?: (node: HastElement) => string | undefined\n}\n```\n\nCallbacks receive the original `pre` node. Language names are read from a `language-*` class on the child `code` element.\n\nFence titles, annotations, and line numbers are read from the child code node's `data.meta`, as emitted by `mdast-util-to-hast`. A callback title or explicit `lineNumbers` option overrides metadata.\n\n## `rehypeHighlightCodeBlocks`\n\n```ts\nfunction rehypeHighlightCodeBlocks(\n  options: RehypeHighlightOptions,\n): (tree: unknown) => void\n```\n\nReturns a synchronous Rehype transformer. It recursively replaces supported `<pre><code>` nodes and skips any `pre` that already has the `th-code` class.\n\n```ts\nimport rehypeStringify from 'rehype-stringify'\nimport remarkParse from 'remark-parse'\nimport remarkRehype from 'remark-rehype'\nimport { unified } from 'unified'\nimport { rehypeHighlightCodeBlocks } from '@tanstack/highlight/rehype'\n\nconst file = await unified()\n  .use(remarkParse)\n  .use(remarkRehype)\n  .use(rehypeHighlightCodeBlocks, { highlighter })\n  .use(rehypeStringify)\n  .process(markdown)\n```\n\n## `rehypePreCodeToHast`\n\n```ts\nfunction rehypePreCodeToHast(\n  node: HastElement,\n  options: RehypeHighlightOptions,\n): HastElement | undefined\n```\n\nConverts one eligible `pre` node. It returns `undefined` when the node is already highlighted or does not contain a direct `code` child. Descendant text is concatenated and trailing whitespace is removed before highlighting.\n\nExisting attributes, classes, and plugin data on the `pre` and `code` elements are preserved.\n\nSee [Markdown Pipelines](../guides/markdown-pipelines) for choosing between the Remark and Rehype integrations.\n"}
